# TopUp Design System

Must follow for all Compose UI in this repo. Native Android only.

## Ownership

- Reusable UI primitives and tokens live in `:core:designsystem`. Features / `shared` / `app` **consume** them.
- No ViewModels, navigation graphs, domain models, or feature business logic in `:core:designsystem`.
- `:core:designsystem` may depend on `:core:common` only — never on `feature/*`, `shared/*`, or `:app`.

## Theme entry

Wrap app UI and previews in `AppTheme { }` (provides Material 3 + TopUp tokens via `AppThemeProvider`).

```kotlin
// ✅
AppTheme { MyScreen() }

// ❌ Raw MaterialTheme / scaffold TopUpTheme / dynamic Material You colors
MaterialTheme { MyScreen() }
```

## Token access (composables)

Read TopUp semantics through `MaterialTheme` extensions — not raw hex colors or `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` for product UI:

| Token | Access |
|-------|--------|
| Colors | `MaterialTheme.appColorScheme` |
| Typography | `MaterialTheme.appTypography` |
| Spacing | `MaterialTheme.appSpacing` |
| Shapes | `MaterialTheme.appShapes` |
| Window class | `MaterialTheme.deviceType` |
| Light/dark | `MaterialTheme.isLightTheme` |

```kotlin
val colors = MaterialTheme.appColorScheme
val spacing = MaterialTheme.appSpacing

Text(
    text = title,
    style = MaterialTheme.appTypography.titleMedium,
    color = colors.contentPrimary,
)
```

## Colors

- Consume by **semantic role** (`primary`, `contentSecondary`, `success`, `error`, …) from `AppColorScheme`.
- Change values only in `AppColorScheme.kt` (`AppLightColorScheme` / `AppDarkColorScheme`). Keep `Theme.kt` Material bridge in sync.
- **Complementary** (gold) is for progress/selection/highlights — not a substitute for `primary` or `success`.
- On neutral surfaces in light theme, prefer `onComplementaryContainer` for complementary-hued labels/icons.
- Do **not** use `Color(0x…)`, `Color.Red`, or Material You dynamic schemes in feature / app UI.

## Typography

- Manrope only (`R.font.manrope_*` in `:core:designsystem`).
- Use `MaterialTheme.appTypography` roles (`displayLarge` … `labelSmall`).
- Do not invent `TextStyle(fontSize = …)` or other font families in features.
- Typography does **not** scale from window width.

## Spacing & shapes

- Fixed primitives / component rhythm (`small`, `button`, `hairline`, …) never scale with window width.
- Adaptive layout tokens (`screenHorizontal`, `section`, `readableMaxWidth`, `bottomNavigationClearance`, …) come from `MaterialTheme.appSpacing` via `getAppSpacing(deviceType)`.
- Add missing spacing to `AppSpacing.kt` — do not hard-code `dp` / `calculatedDp` in screens.
- Use `AppSpacing.Default` only in non-composable defaults — never for screen layout.
- Corners: `MaterialTheme.appShapes` — not ad-hoc `RoundedCornerShape(12.dp)`.
- Window decisions: `MaterialTheme.deviceType` / `DeviceWidthClass` only — not `LocalConfiguration` breakpoints in features.

## Components

- Public composables: `App*` (e.g. `AppPrimaryButton`). Shared constants: `App*Defaults`.
- Structure: `components/<category>/` under `:core:designsystem`; build on Material 3.
- Accept `modifier: Modifier = Modifier`; hoist state/callbacks to callers.
- Previews: wrap in `AppTheme { }`; exercise light/dark when useful.

## When to extend

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Used in 2+ features or generic pattern | Add/extend `:core:designsystem` |
| Single-screen layout only | Feature `presentation/components` using design-system tokens |
| New color / spacing / type role | Add to theme files first, then consume |
